  "helpTitle": "Help",
  "helpQ1": "What is SENTINEL?",
  "helpA1": "SENTINEL is your personal safety companion. It allows you to set a timer and if you don't check in before it expires, it automatically alerts your emergency contacts with your last known location and a custom message.",
  "helpQ2": "How do I create a new SENTINEL?",
  "helpA2": "Tap the '+' button on the home screen. Set a duration (e.g., 30 minutes), add any notes or files, and select your emergency contacts. Tap 'Initiate SENTINEL' to start.",
  "helpQ3": "What happens when the timer expires?",
  "helpA3": "When the timer reaches zero, SENTINEL immediately notifies all your selected emergency contacts via SMS/Email. They will receive your custom message and a link to view your last known location on a map.",
  "helpQ4": "What is a 'Check-In'?",
  "helpA4": "Checking in cancels the active countdown. Use this once you are safe or no longer need the SENTINEL. If you check in, no alerts will be sent.",
  "helpQ5": "Can I extend an active timer?",
  "helpA5": "Yes! Tap on your active SENTINEL and use the 'Extend' button to add more time if your situation changes.",
  "helpQ6": "Who are emergency contacts?",
  "helpA6": "Emergency contacts are people you trust. You must select at least one contact for every SENTINEL. You can manage your contacts in the 'Contacts' screen accessible from the drawer.",
  "helpQ7": "Does SENTINEL track my location?",
  "helpA7": "SENTINEL ONLY tracks your location while a timer is active. We value your privacy and do not monitor your movements when the app is idle or no SENTINELs are running.",
  "helpQ8": "What if I have no internet?",
  "helpA8": "SENTINEL requires an internet connection to initiate an event and upload data. If you lose connection during an active event, the countdown on our servers will still trigger the alert unless you check in.",
  "helpQ9": "How many contacts can I add?",
  "helpA9": "You can add up to 10 emergency contacts per SENTINEL event.",
  "helpQ10": "Is my data secure?",
  "helpA10": "Yes, your personal data and location are encrypted. Only the emergency contacts you specify can see your location, and only after an alert is triggered.",
  "helpQ11": "Can I add photos or recordings?",
  "helpA11": "Yes! When creating a SENTINEL, you can attach files. These will be shared with your contacts if the alert is triggered, providing more context about your situation.",
  "helpQ12": "What is the 'I AM SAFE' button?",
  "helpA12": "This is your check-in button. Tapping it tells SENTINEL that you are okay, which immediately stops the countdown and prevents any alerts from being sent.",
  "helpQ13": "Does the app need to be open?",
  "helpA13": "No. SENTINEL runs its critical countdown on our secure servers. Even if your phone dies, loses battery, or is destroyed, the alert will still be sent when the timer expires.",
  "helpQ14": "How do I manage my profile?",
  "helpA14": "You can update your name and see your account details in the 'Profile' section, accessible from the app drawer.",
  "helpQ15": "What if I trigger an alert by mistake?",
  "helpA15": "If an alert is sent, your contacts will be notified. We recommend contacting them immediately to let them know it was a false alarm. Always try to check in BEFORE the timer reaches zero.",
